│ Two real problems in the fingerprint re-key and one nit. The migration path is otherwise sound.  │|
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯|
                                                                                                    |
CRITICAL ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────|
▌ src/auth/fingerprint.rs:42 · bug · conf 90                                                        |
▌ Re-key drops sessions created during the migration window                                         |
▌ The loop reads the old key once and writes the new one after every batch, so sessions created mid-|
▌ run keep the old fingerprint.                                                                     |
▌ ▾ failure scenario                                                                                |
▌   A user logs in while the re-key runs; their next request fails the fingerprint check and they   |
▌   are signed out.                                                                                 |
▌ ▾ suggestion                                                                                      |
▌   Take the write lock for the whole re-key, or re-read the key per batch.                         |
                                                                                                    |
HIGH ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────|
│ src/auth/store.rs:118 · concurrency · conf 75                                                     |
│ Unbounded retry on lock contention                                                                |
